  "typeScale": {
    "$description": "Real-size scale (window 1100x720): body 13 = meta / metaTight, secondary 12 = small / smallTight, micro 11 = tag (microNote: the same with the 1.45 line of the offline panel), page title 24/300 = pageTitle (line 1.2), section 18/300 = cardTitle, onboarding headline 28/300 = onbTitle, onboarding subtitle and device name 14 = bodySm, group title of the settings 16 = body, wordmark 15/600 = wordmark (onboarding brand 14/600 = wordmarkSm), recording timer 44 = timer, Geist Mono numbers 12 = monoRow and font.mono, Geist Mono 11 (kbd, timecodes) = monoSmall, Geist Mono 10 = caption. The *Tight entries are the line heights Chromium gives one line of the canvas ('normal'). Tracking: the canvas sets letter-spacing 0.01em once on the 13 px page, so every Inter / Geist Mono run inherits 0.13 px whatever its size ('letterSpacing' 0.13 absolute); the display entries and the wordmarks have their own em (-0.02 / -0.01). messageLine (13), sourceSnippet (12) and credit (12) are the Ask AI answer and Session transcript text, the Ask AI source and the About credit texts at the whole-pixel lines 20, 17 and 19: Avalonia's layout rounding makes the canvas lines of 20.15, 17.4 and 19.2 one pixel taller each. noteMicro (11, line 1.55 = 17.05) is the note under the cards of the Recording screen.",
