  "glassOrbs": {
    "$description": "The canvas orbs painted by GlassOrbControl with the orbGradient above: the recording orb and the onboarding's welcome and voice orbs. 'size' is the control's side in px, 'body' the sphere's diameter as a share of it, 'glowBlur' the blur of the white inner glow (CSS box-shadow: inset 0 0 Npx), 'haloBlur' the standard deviation of the halo's Gaussian blur (CSS blur(Npx)), 'haloOpacity' its opacity, 'glow' the opacity of the inner glow. haloBlur, haloOpacity and glow differ between the themes: each has a 'Dark' twin that is required (the generator refuses an entry without it); size, body and glowBlur are the same in both. An orb that breathes (the welcome orb, canvas 'halo' key frames) may give 'breathHaloScale' (the halo's scale at the peak of the breath) and 'breathHaloFade' (the share of its rest opacity the halo loses at the peak: light .32 to .10 is 0.6875, dark .5 to .2 is 0.6), each with its 'Dark' twin.",
